IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `epd-nouns`

-- The ePrivacy Directive (Directive 2002/58/EC), consolidated version of 19.12.2009: Articles 5 and 6.
-- LAYER 1. Confidentiality of the communications (Art 5) and traffic data (Art 6).
-- An EXCEPTION is answered in the polarity of the rule it limits: "shall not prevent X" is a rule named "the paragraph
-- prevents X", which answers JUST FALSE inside the exception and NOTHING outside it (NOTES.md, "Reading a result").

§ `Article 5 -- confidentiality of the communications`

-- src:74 | Member States shall ensure the confidentiality of communications and the related traffic data by means of a public communications network and publicly available electronic communications services, through national legislation.
@ref Art 5(1) first sentence (src:74) row:A5(1).s1
GIVEN `the thing is a communication, or traffic data related to a communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is by means of a public communications network or a publicly available electronic communications service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1) first sentence the Directive requires the confidentiality of the communication and the related traffic data` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a communication, or traffic data related to a communication` AND `it is by means of a public communications network or a publicly available electronic communications service`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence names communications and related traffic data by means of public networks and publicly available services
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:74 | In particular, they shall prohibit listening, tapping, storage or other kinds of interception or surveillance of communications and the related traffic data by persons other than users, without the consent of the users concerned, except when legally authorised to do so in accordance with Article 15(1).
@ref Art 5(1) second sentence (src:74) row:A5(1).s2
GIVEN `the act is listening, tapping, storage or another kind of interception or surveillance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is of communications or of the related traffic data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is by a person other than a user` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the users concerned have consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is legally authorised to do so in accordance with Article 15(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1) second sentence the Directive requires the act to be prohibited` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is stated for those acts, on communications and related traffic data, by persons other than users
        IF NOT `the act is listening, tapping, storage or another kind of interception or surveillance` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the prohibition is stated for communications and the related traffic data
        IF NOT `the act is of communications or of the related traffic data` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by persons other than users" -- an act by a user is outside the prohibition's words
        IF NOT `the act is by a person other than a user` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except when legally authorised to do so in accordance with Article 15(1)" -- an "except" once met, decided case by case (FORK F12)
        IF `the person is legally authorised to do so in accordance with Article 15(1)` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without the consent of the users concerned" -- where the users concerned have consented the prohibition's words do not reach the act
        IF `the users concerned have consented` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same prohibition as a regulative rule: the person intercepting SHANT intercept. The text fixes no time.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Directive` `Act under the Directive`
`Art 5(1) second sentence the person intercepting shall not intercept the communication` MEANS
    PARTY `the person intercepting`
    SHANT `intercept the communication`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person intercepting` BECAUSE "Art 5(1) second sentence: listening, tapping, storage or other interception or surveillance without the consent of the users concerned"

-- src:74 | This paragraph shall not prevent technical storage which is necessary for the conveyance of a communication without prejudice to the principle of confidentiality.
@ref Art 5(1) third sentence (src:74) row:A5(1).s3
GIVEN `the storage is technical storage which is necessary for the conveyance of a communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the storage is without prejudice to the principle of confidentiality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(1) third sentence the paragraph prevents the storage` MEANS
    IF `the storage is technical storage which is necessary for the conveyance of a communication` AND `the storage is without prejudice to the principle of confidentiality`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This paragraph shall not prevent technical storage which is necessary for the conveyance of a communication"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shall not prevent technical storage which is necessary for the conveyance of a communication" speaks only of that storage
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:75 | Paragraph 1 shall not affect any legally authorised recording of communications and the related traffic data when carried out in the course of lawful business practice for the purpose of providing evidence of a commercial transaction or of any other business communication.
@ref Art 5(2) (src:75) row:A5(2)
GIVEN `the recording is legally authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recording is of communications and the related traffic data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recording is carried out in the course of lawful business practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the recording is for the purpose of providing evidence of a commercial transaction or of any other business communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(2) paragraph 1 affects the recording` MEANS
    IF `the recording is legally authorised` AND `the recording is of communications and the related traffic data` AND `the recording is carried out in the course of lawful business practice` AND `the recording is for the purpose of providing evidence of a commercial transaction or of any other business communication`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph 1 shall not affect any legally authorised recording of communications and the related traffic data"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when carried out in the course of lawful business practice for the purpose of providing evidence" -- outside those words the paragraph does not say that Article 5(1) is unaffected
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:77 | Member States shall ensure that the storing of information, or the gaining of access to information already stored, in the terminal equipment of a subscriber or user is only allowed on condition that the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent, having been provided with clear and comprehensive information, in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC, inter alia, about the purposes of the processing.
@ref Art 5(3) first sentence (src:77) row:A5(3).s1
GIVEN `the act is the storing of information, or the gaining of access to information already stored, in the terminal equipment of a subscriber or user` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(3) first sentence the storing or access is only allowed on condition of consent` MEANS
    IF `the act is the storing of information, or the gaining of access to information already stored, in the terminal equipment of a subscriber or user`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about storing or gaining access in the terminal equipment of a subscriber or user
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:77 | is only allowed on condition that the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent, having been provided with clear and comprehensive information, in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC, inter alia, about the purposes of the processing.
@ref Art 5(3) first sentence (src:77) row:A5(3).s1
GIVEN `the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber or user was provided with clear and comprehensive information, inter alia about the purposes of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consent and the information are in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(3) first sentence the condition of consent is met` MEANS
    IF `the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent`
       AND `the subscriber or user was provided with clear and comprehensive information, inter alia about the purposes of the processing`
       AND `the consent and the information are in accordance with Directive 95/46/EC`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is only allowed on condition that the subscriber or user concerned has given his or her consent"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:77 | This shall not prevent any technical storage or access for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network, or as strictly necessary in order for the provider of an information society service explicitly requested by the subscriber or user to provide the service.
@ref Art 5(3) second sentence (src:77) row:A5(3).s2
GIVEN `it is technical storage or access` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider of an information society service was explicitly requested by the subscriber or user to provide the service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the storage or access is strictly necessary in order for that provider to provide the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 5(3) second sentence the first sentence prevents the storage or access` MEANS
    IF `it is technical storage or access`
       AND (   `it is for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication over an electronic communications network`
            OR (`the provider of an information society service was explicitly requested by the subscriber or user to provide the service` AND `the storage or access is strictly necessary in order for that provider to provide the service`))
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This shall not prevent any technical storage or access for the sole purpose of carrying out the transmission of a communication"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "sole purpose", "strictly necessary" and "explicitly requested" bound the exception; outside them the sentence is silent
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Article 6 -- traffic data`

-- src:81 | Traffic data relating to subscribers and users processed and stored by the provider of a public communications network or publicly available electronic communications service must be erased or made anonymous when it is no longer needed for the purpose of the transmission of a communication without prejudice to paragraphs 2, 3 and 5 of this Article and Article 15(1).
@ref Art 6(1) (src:81) row:A6(1)
GIVEN `the data is traffic data relating to subscribers and users, processed and stored by the provider of a public communications network or publicly available electronic communications service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data is no longer needed for the purpose of the transmission of a communication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph 2, 3 or 5 of this Article or Article 15(1) applies to the data` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(1) the provider must erase the traffic data or make it anonymous` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is about traffic data relating to subscribers and users processed and stored by the provider
        IF NOT `the data is traffic data relating to subscribers and users, processed and stored by the provider of a public communications network or publicly available electronic communications service` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when it is no longer needed for the purpose of the transmission of a communication" -- a "when" condition that fails (periods ruling (b), (c)); FORK F6
        IF NOT `the data is no longer needed for the purpose of the transmission of a communication` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without prejudice to paragraphs 2, 3 and 5 of this Article and Article 15(1)" -- what those provisions allow is not decided here
        IF `paragraph 2, 3 or 5 of this Article or Article 15(1) applies to the data` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same duty as a regulative rule. The text says "when it is no longer needed", so there is no separate deadline.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Directive` `Act under the Directive`
`Art 6(1) the provider erases the traffic data or makes it anonymous` MEANS
    PARTY `the provider`
    MUST `erase the traffic data or make it anonymous`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the provider` BECAUSE "Art 6(1): the traffic data was not erased or made anonymous when it was no longer needed for the transmission of a communication"

-- src:82 | Traffic data necessary for the purposes of subscriber billing and interconnection payments may be processed.
-- src:82 | Such processing is permissible only up to the end of the period during which the bill may lawfully be challenged or payment pursued.
@ref Art 6(2) (src:82) row:A6(2).s1 row:A6(2).s2
GIVEN `the data is necessary for the purposes of subscriber billing and interconnection payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the processing` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period during which the bill may lawfully be challenged or payment pursued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(2) the processing of the traffic data for billing is permissible on the date` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is about traffic data necessary for subscriber billing and interconnection payments
        IF NOT `the data is necessary for the purposes of subscriber billing and interconnection payments` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Such processing is permissible only up to the end of the period during which the bill may lawfully be challenged or payment pursued" -- FORK F23: the last day of the period is inside it
        IF `the date of the processing` GREATER THAN `the last day of the period during which the bill may lawfully be challenged or payment pursued` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:84 | For the purpose of marketing electronic communications services or for the provision of value added services, the provider of a publicly available electronic communications service may process the data referred to in paragraph 1 to the extent and for the duration necessary for such services or marketing, if the subscriber or user to whom the data relate has given his or her prior consent.
@ref Art 6(3) first sentence (src:84) row:A6(3).s1
GIVEN `the purpose is marketing electronic communications services or the provision of value added services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subscriber or user to whom the data relate has given his or her prior consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the processing is to the extent and for the duration necessary for such services or marketing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(3) first sentence the provider may process the traffic data` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the permission is stated for the purpose of marketing electronic communications services or the provision of value added services
        IF NOT `the purpose is marketing electronic communications services or the provision of value added services` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the subscriber or user to whom the data relate has given his or her prior consent` AND `the processing is to the extent and for the duration necessary for such services or marketing` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a "may" grant whose "if" gate failed; the text does not close the gate with "only" (grant and power ruling item 1; FORK F13)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:84 | Users or subscribers shall be given the possibility to withdraw their consent for the processing of traffic data at any time.
@ref Art 6(3) second sentence (src:84) row:A6(3).s2
GIVEN `the consent was given for the processing of traffic data under paragraph 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(3) second sentence the user or subscriber has the possibility to withdraw the consent at any time` MEANS
    IF `the consent was given for the processing of traffic data under paragraph 3`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about consent for the processing of traffic data
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:86 | The service provider must inform the subscriber or user of the types of traffic data which are processed and of the duration of such processing for the purposes mentioned in paragraph 2 and, prior to obtaining consent, for the purposes mentioned in paragraph 3.
@ref Art 6(4) (src:86) row:A6(4)
GIVEN `the purpose is one mentioned in paragraph 2 or paragraph 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(4) the provider must inform the subscriber or user` MEANS
    IF `the purpose is one mentioned in paragraph 2 or paragraph 3`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is stated for the purposes mentioned in paragraphs 2 and 3
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:86 | The service provider must inform the subscriber or user of the types of traffic data which are processed and of the duration of such processing for the purposes mentioned in paragraph 2 and, prior to obtaining consent, for the purposes mentioned in paragraph 3.
@ref Art 6(4) (src:86) row:A6(4)
GIVEN `the purpose is the one mentioned in paragraph 3 (marketing, or value added services)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider informed the subscriber or user of the types of traffic data which are processed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider informed the subscriber or user of the duration of such processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider did so prior to obtaining consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(4) the provider's duty to inform the subscriber or user is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must inform the subscriber or user of the types of traffic data which are processed and of the duration of such processing"
        IF (NOT `the provider informed the subscriber or user of the types of traffic data which are processed`) OR (NOT `the provider informed the subscriber or user of the duration of such processing`) THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prior to obtaining consent, for the purposes mentioned in paragraph 3"
        IF `the purpose is the one mentioned in paragraph 3 (marketing, or value added services)` AND (NOT `the provider did so prior to obtaining consent`) THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:87 | Processing of traffic data, in accordance with paragraphs 1, 2, 3 and 4, must be restricted to persons acting under the authority of providers of the public communications networks and publicly available electronic communications services handling billing or traffic management, customer enquiries, fraud detection, marketing electronic communications services or providing a value added service, and must be restricted to what is necessary for the purposes of such activities.
@ref Art 6(5) (src:87) row:A6(5)
GIVEN `the processing is by a person acting under the authority of a provider of a public communications network or publicly available electronic communications service` IS A BOOLEAN
      activity IS A `Traffic data activity`
      `the processing is restricted to what is necessary for the purposes of such activities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(5) the processing of the traffic data is restricted as required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be restricted to persons acting under the authority of providers of the public communications networks and publicly available electronic communications services" -- FORK F14: "must be restricted to" read as closing the persons
        IF NOT `the processing is by a person acting under the authority of a provider of a public communications network or publicly available electronic communications service` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "handling billing or traffic management, customer enquiries, fraud detection, marketing electronic communications services or providing a value added service" -- FORK F14: the list read as closed by "must be restricted to"
        IF activity EQUALS `another activity` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be restricted to what is necessary for the purposes of such activities"
        IF NOT `the processing is restricted to what is necessary for the purposes of such activities` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:88 | Paragraphs 1, 2, 3 and 5 shall apply without prejudice to the possibility for competent bodies to be informed of traffic data in conformity with applicable legislation with a view to settling disputes, in particular interconnection or billing disputes.
@ref Art 6(6) (src:88) row:A6(6)
GIVEN `the body is a competent body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is informed of traffic data in conformity with applicable legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is informed with a view to settling disputes, in particular interconnection or billing disputes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 6(6) the competent body may be informed of the traffic data` MEANS
    IF `the body is a competent body` AND `it is informed of traffic data in conformity with applicable legislation` AND `it is informed with a view to settling disputes, in particular interconnection or billing disputes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the possibility is preserved for competent bodies, in conformity with applicable legislation, with a view to settling disputes
    ELSE NOTHING
